## 9. Prevention

*Concrete actions to stop this type of defect happening again. Group by area and give each an owner if possible.*

| Area | Action | Owner |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Requirements** | [e.g. Write edge cases into the spec explicitly: "What happens when no previous record exists?"; include time windows in the functional spec; get client sign-off on scope and on a manual process flowchart] | [Name / role] |
| **Pre-implementation** | [e.g. Hold a walkthrough with developer, QA and product owner to agree expected behavior, fallback conditions and data dependencies] | |
| **Test design** | [e.g. Expand test scope to include next-day and later data; include other user types; include actions done ahead of time] | |
| **Retesting after bug fixes** | [e.g. Agree the retest scope with the developer for every fix; keep a user-story checklist for quick rechecks before UAT and release] | |
| **Code review** | [e.g. Question any change to data types; check every part of the system that writes to a table before relying on it] | |
| **Release process** | [e.g. Release non-urgent patches that touch the same module on the same branch/date to avoid merge conflicts] | |
| **Monitoring** | [e.g. Watch application logs for errors during testing and production checks] | |

