## 10. Classification

| Item | Value | Reason |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Severity level** | Critical / Major / Minor / Trivial | [e.g. "Major – core requirement of the scheduled job; 2 users affected"] |
| **Counted against system usability / availability?** | YES / NO | [e.g. "NO – no downtime; only data records affected and corrected the same day"] |
| **Counted in Defect Detection Percentage (DDP)?** | YES / NO | [YES if testing should have caught it; NO if the behavior was not in the original requirements] |

### Business interruption check
*Counted as a business interruption only if **all four** criteria are YES.*

| Criterion | Guidance | Answer | Reason |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **1. Interrupted normal operations?** | Affected core operations, e.g. session management, payments/fees, the application itself, delivery of the service | YES / NO | |
| **2. Needed a release to resolve?** | Has workaround + release done → YES <br> Has workaround + no release → NO <br> No workaround + release done → YES | YES / NO | |
| **3. Needed extra attention?** | An emergency chat/war room was created, or extra people / other teams had to help | YES / NO | |
| **4. High number of reports?** | Number of reported incidents is high compared with the normal trend | YES / NO | |
| **Result: Business interruption?** | | **YES / NO** | |

