## Appendix A — Filled-in example (anonymized)

| Field | Details |
| --- | --- |
| **Title** | [1H 2025] – Booked slots disabled after user opens the lesson notes page |
| **Affected service** | User-facing web portal |
| **Problem** | After a user opened the lesson notes page, an already-booked slot became disabled on the schedule page, even though it was still within the allowed cancellation window. |
| **Cause** | A new log entry was written the first time the notes page was opened. It updated a status flag, which reset the "1 hour since booking" calculation. |
| **Impact** | Users had to ask the operations team to close the slot, which undid one of the project's goals (reducing requests to operations). |
| **Reporter** | Project team |
| **Timeline** | Deployed 09:47 → reported 10:30 next day → quick fix 11:38 → fix released 15:00. **Duration: 4 hrs 30 mins** |
| **Workaround** | Close the slot via the admin scheduler, or wait 1 hour after first opening the notes page. |
| **Resolution** | Added a check on the flag in the log table. |
| **Prevention** | When relying on logs, check every part of the system that writes to that table. Add "open lesson notes ahead of time" to test scenarios. |
| **Severity** | Minor |
| **Counted in DDP?** | YES – the schedule page wasn't rechecked after opening the notes page during spot checks. |
| **Business interruption?** | NO – workaround available and only the project team reported it. |
